<title>SRI LANKA: Weather-Light showers seen over most of Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>Weather-Light showers seen over most of Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's metereological department released the following rainfall figures for 24 hours ending Friday morning</p>
<p>Hydro catchment areas (in mm):</p>
<p>    Bowathenna		0</p>
<p>    Canyon		    0</p>
<p>    Castlereigh	     0</p>
<p>    Kotmale		   0</p>
<p>    Laxapana		  0</p>
<p>    Moussakele		2.2</p>
<p>    Norton		    0</p>
<p>    Randenigala	     0</p>
<p>    Victoria		  0</p>
<p>    Samanalawewa	    0</p>
<p>    Ukuwela		   0</p>
<p>    Rantembe		  0</p>
<p>The department forecast occaisional showers and fairly strong winds in the Western, Central and Sabaragamuwa provinces and in the Galle and Matara districts and light showers over the rest of the island on Saturday.</p>
</text>
